395 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 304 0 R
/T (MicroED-Guided Structural Elucidation of Secondary Metabolites from Natural Sources)
/E (MicroED-Guided Structural Elucidation of Secondary Metabolites from Natural Sources)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
396 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 304 0 R
/T ( What is your research topic?)
/E ( What is your research topic?)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
397 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1081 0 R
/E (My research topic is MicroED-Guided Structural Elucidation of Secondary Metabolites from Natural Sources. What I do in very simple terms is I take plants, extract out the natural compounds, crystallize them, put them in a transmission electron microscope \(TEM\) and shoot electrons at the crystals, collecting movies while doing so. I then take the movies and process the data, which is then put in Olex2 to elucidate the 3D crystal structure in order to refine the structure. After determining the structure, the compound can be tested for antimicrobial properties which is helpful for growing antimicrobial resistance \(AMR\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
398 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 304 0 R
/T ( What inspired you to pursue this topic?)
/E ( What inspired you to pursue this topic?)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1082 0 R
/E (My mom is a chemistry professor at UCLA, and she went to Caltech for graduate school. She would always talk to me about how great her experience was there, describing Caltech as a place that makes you want to research all of the time since everyone there is super passionate about science. After working last summer at UCLA under Professor Abigail Doyle I was so inspired that I wanted to continue researching and to explore a new area of chemistry. When thinking about what topic I could focus on, I found Professor Hosea Nelson and became interested in MicroED. Specifically, I became interested in different plants and looking up their secondary metabolites, which led me to look for newly discovered plants.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 304 0 R
/T ( What impact do you hope your research will have?)
/E ( What impact do you hope your research will have?)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
401 0 obj
<<
