/T (Have there been any challenges or unexpected moments during your journey? If not, something you have learned?)
/E (Have there been any challenges or unexpected moments during your journey? If not, something you have learned?)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
451 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 308 0 R
/T (Initially my entire research was going to be qualitative focused. However, I realized that none of my data would be statistically significant because my control size is only 8 people which meant that any quantitative data would only be applicable to those individuals. At first, I was terrified that my entire research project would fall apart. So to fix my issue, I decided to switch gears and took on a more qualitative approach, changing my research question and deciding to interview both the tutors and tutees. With qualitative data, you can understand every individual's perspective in depth and really understand nuanced outlooks on the situation rather than relying on patterns to generalize findings. In a lot of ways, qualitative data is more meaningful than quantitative data and now I am happy with my decision to switch.)
/E (Initially my entire research was going to be qualitative focused. However, I realized that none of my data would be statistically significant because my control size is only 8 people which meant that any quantitative data would only be applicable to those individuals. At first, I was terrified that my entire research project would fall apart. So to fix my issue, I decided to switch gears and took on a more qualitative approach, changing my research question and deciding to interview both the tutors and tutees. With qualitative data, you can understand every individual's perspective in depth and really understand nuanced outlooks on the situation rather than relying on patterns to generalize findings. In a lot of ways, qualitative data is more meaningful than quantitative data and now I am happy with my decision to switch.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
