1606 0 obj
<<
/Title (I was lucky enough to find my mentor at an AI related event that I went to, so that was my first step. I think the most important first step, however, is to find the question that I wanted to study. To do so, I looked into Science Direct, Google Scholar, and JSTOR to find the gaps in my research topic and then decided my research question from there. With these sources I made summaries of them and put them into my bibliography to make it easier to write my lit review. Then I would email a mentor and tell them about the overall idea I would be thinking of, generate my materials, and get started.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1596 0 R
>>
endobj
